<title>FRANCE: Casino, Promodes shares active on bid speculation.</title>
<headline>Casino, Promodes shares active on bid speculation.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Casino and Promodes, widely rumoured to be potential merger candidates, were active on Thursday, but the companies both declined to make any comment.</p>
<p>Bid speculation was fanned by the announcement on Wednesday that Carrefour, the biggest French retailer, had taken a 33 percent stake in the holding company of the Cora hypermarkets chain.</p>
<p>Shares in Casino were up 2.33 percent, while Promodes -- widely viewed as the suitor -- were down 1.15 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
